    "description": "Tree farm, level 3 of 3: L2 plus flourish 3. Over budget: 344 blocks vs 102 (the lumber camp brief; the tree farm has no budget of its own), first build 268 vs 200; 19 x 14 instead of 11 x 11 because the yard moved outside the plot. The lumber camp's tier-6 upgrade: a fenced planting plot (11 x 13, spruce fence on capped cobblestone piers, a timber gateway) holding only three raised dirt rows and lanes, saplings 3 apart with open sky above; beside it, outside the fence, the woodcutter's yard: a 5 x 4 gabled shed in the sawmill's look (oak door; chest, grindstone workstation, barrel), a log pile, chopping block, composter, cobblestone slab paths. L1: plot with empty rows, shed, yard. L2: oak, birch and spruce saplings in the rows, a lychgate roof with lanterns, lanterns on the piers, shutters, a sawhorse, a cauldron and barrel by the gate. L3: a lean-to drying shed over the logs, a hanging sign (the Studio does not draw hanging signs), banners by the shed door, potted saplings on a shelf, flowers along the outside of the fence, moss, an axe in the block. Not yet builder-tested: azure_bluet, birch_sapling, cauldron, cornflower, dandelion, green_wall_banner, moss_carpet, oak_hanging_sign, oak_sapling, oxeye_daisy, spruce_sapling. Decoration step adds: item_frame, potted_plant, sign_text.",
    "changes": "Carlton's note: \"Take decoration from the inside and put them outside make sure the place where the sapling sit are clear cause other sapling will sit there and grow\". The fenced plot now holds only three raised dirt rows and the walking lanes between them: the young trees, bushes and every prop are gone from it. Saplings (oak, birch, spruce) come at L2, each 3 blocks from the next, with nothing above them (no leaves, roofs or lanterns over the rows); at L1 the rows are empty dirt. Shed, log pile, chopping block, composter, sawhorse, drying lean-to, cauldron, barrels, banners and flowers moved outside the fence: into a woodcutter's yard on the right, by the gate and along the fence.",
